<title>USA: Allergan has FDA clearance to market Tazorac.</title>
<headline>Allergan has FDA clearance to market Tazorac.</headline>
<dateline>IRVINE, Calif. 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Allergan Inc said on Monday that the U.S. Food and Drug Administration has approved its application to market Tazorac 0.05 percent and 0.1 percent in the United States.</p>
<p>The company said the topical gel is used for the treatment of stable plaque psoriasis afflicting up to 20 percent of body surface. Also, the 0.1 percent gel may be used for mild-to-moderately severe facial acne vulgaris.</p>
<p>The company said clinical trials have shown the drug to be effective in up to 70 percent of patients.</p>
</text>
